From: Security Audit <audit@ka9q-radio.local>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Fix lmalloc() assert to proper error handling

The lmalloc() function uses assert() for error handling, which is
removed in release builds (-DNDEBUG). This causes silent failures
and NULL pointer dereferences when memory allocation fails.

Replace assert() with proper error handling that works in both
debug and release builds.

Bug: Critical - NULL pointer dereference in production
Risk: System crash on out-of-memory conditions
---
 src/misc.c | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/misc.c b/src/misc.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/misc.c
+++ b/src/misc.c
@@ -1025,12 +1025,10 @@ long hugepagesize(void){
 void *lmalloc(size_t size){
   void *ptr;
   int r;
-  if((r = posix_memalign(&ptr,64,size)) == 0){
-    assert(ptr != NULL);
+  if((r = posix_memalign(&ptr, 64, size)) == 0 && ptr != NULL){
     return ptr;
   }
-  errno = r;
-  assert(false);
+  errno = (r != 0) ? r : ENOMEM;
   return NULL;
 }

